# Text / number overflow — resize, don’t leave overlaps

If a digit, label, caption, or other text **overlaps** or collides with another element (icon, separator, neighbour label, tile edge), **reduce its font size** (or truncate / clip as a last resort) so the layout stays readable.

## Do

- Detect likely collisions: long numbers (`1 248`), long FR/EN labels, tight HBox rows, donut centre copy
- Prefer a **slightly smaller font** that fits over leaving a visual overlap
- Keep hierarchy: shrink the overflowing value first; only shrink neighbours if needed
- On profile tiles, shrink **inside** the tile — never widen the tile or page gutters to “make room” (see `profile-tile-width.mdc`)

## Don’t

- Ship overlapping text as acceptable by default
- Fix overlap by changing locked profile tile / page **widths** unless the user asks
- Scale the whole tile just to fit one label
